From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:50:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 
 fat-roll-back-the-new-entry-when-create-mkdir-fails-to-build-the-inode-fix

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: OGAWA Hirofumi <hirofumi@mail.parknet.co.jp>
Cc: zhoumin <teczm@foxmail.com>
---
 fs/fat/misc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/fat/misc.c b/fs/fat/misc.c
index c44296756eae6..0a1ee90353276 100644
--- a/fs/fat/misc.c
+++ b/fs/fat/misc.c
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ void _fat_msg(struct super_block *sb, const char *level, const char *fmt, ...)
 	_printk(FAT_PRINTK_PREFIX "%pV\n", level, sb->s_id, &vaf);
 	va_end(args);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_fat_msg);
 
 /* Flushes the number of free clusters on FAT32 */
 /* XXX: Need to write one per FSINFO block.  Currently only writes 1 */
